  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILF for WASH Foundational Support (IMM &amp; IR) for Nazava Water Filters Limited</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale - TA for Impact-Linked Finance for WASH (ILF for WASH)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Foundational Support Programme is one of the [technical assistance](https://aquaforall.org/ilf-for-wash/ilf-for-wash-technical-assistance/) tracks available for impact-driven WASH enterprises, as part of the Impact-Linked Fund for Water, Sanitation and Hygiene ([ILF for WASH](https://aquaforall.org/ilf-for-wash/)). The programme is supported by the [Social Finance Academy,](https://social-finance-academy.org/) an initiative by Roots of Impact.The programme aims to transfer knowledge and skills from certified service providers to WASH enterprises in two areas: impact measurement and management (IMM) and investment readiness (IR). At the same time, the goal is to embed these areas into the specific business model of the selected enterprises.One of the selected enterprises receiving support on both IMM and IR is Nazava Water Filters Limited (Kenya). Nazava Water Filters manufactures simple &amp; affordable, household water filters that are certified by the WHO and KEBS for bacterial removal.</narrative>
  </description>
